We offer our resources to the local body of Christ as an expression of gratitude and trust in our generous God, who has freely given us all things—above all, his grace. As Paul writes, “For you know the grace of our Lord Jesus Christ, that though he was rich, yet for your sake he became poor, so that you by his poverty might become rich” (2 Corinthians 8:9).

A healthy church depends on the faithful generosity of those who call it home. Through our shared giving, the church is able to worship, serve, and participate in God’s mission.

Why do we share what we’ve been given? Jesus’ words say it simply and beautifully: “Freely you have received; freely give” (Matthew 10:8).
